# fal.ai CDN media (mandatory)

Vista 3 output formats are `post` (image) and `reel` (video). fal.ai generates both. Files live on the fal CDN (`https://v3b.fal.media/...`). Convex stores **URL strings + status**, never the blob.

- fal calls belong in Convex **actions** only.
- Preview: `<img src={imageUrl} />` / `<video src={videoUrl} />`.
- Live publish: download from the fal URL at publish time. Do not copy into `_storage` first.
- Do not add `videoStorageId` or `imageStorageId` for fal output. ElevenLabs audio may still use `_storage`.
- Platforms stay `"x" | "linkedin"` unless the schema union is extended. `reel` is a format, not Instagram/TikTok.

```ts
// BAD — never persist fal output in Convex storage
imageStorageId: v.optional(v.id("_storage")),
videoStorageId: v.optional(v.id("_storage")),
await ctx.storage.store(blob);

// GOOD
format: v.union(v.literal("post"), v.literal("reel")),
imageUrl: v.optional(v.string()),
videoUrl: v.optional(v.string()),
```
